WEBVTT

00:00.850 --> 00:03.590
Everyone in the kingdom is very
impressed with your ability

00:03.590 --> 00:06.380
to help with the party
planning, everyone

00:06.380 --> 00:09.330
except for this gentlemen
right over here.

00:09.330 --> 00:11.140
This is Arbegla.

00:11.140 --> 00:13.840
And he is the
king's top adviser,

00:13.840 --> 00:15.890
and also chief party planner.

00:15.890 --> 00:18.010
And he seems somewhat
threatened by your ability

00:18.010 --> 00:20.752
to solve these otherwise
unsolvable problems,

00:20.752 --> 00:22.210
or at least from
his point of view,

00:22.210 --> 00:24.740
because he keeps over-ordering
or under-ordering things

00:24.740 --> 00:26.110
like cupcakes.

00:26.110 --> 00:30.150
And he says, king, that
cupcake problem was easy.

00:30.150 --> 00:32.870
Ask them about the
potato chip issue,

00:32.870 --> 00:35.330
because we could never get
the potato chips right.

00:35.330 --> 00:37.820
And so the king says,
Arbegla, that's a good idea.

00:37.820 --> 00:39.520
We need to get the
potato chips right.

00:39.520 --> 00:41.420
So he comes to you
and says, how do we

00:41.420 --> 00:44.119
figure out, on average, how many
potato chips we need to order?

00:44.119 --> 00:45.660
And to do that, we
have to figure out

00:45.660 --> 00:47.910
how much, on average,
does each man eat

00:47.910 --> 00:49.670
and how much each woman eats.

00:49.670 --> 00:51.606
You say, well, what
about the children?

00:51.606 --> 00:52.980
The king says, in
our kingdom, we

00:52.980 --> 00:55.560
forbid potato
chips for children.

00:55.560 --> 00:58.400
You say, oh, well,
that's all and good.

00:58.400 --> 01:01.070
Tell me what happened
at the previous parties.

01:01.070 --> 01:03.940
And so the king says, you might
remember, at the last party,

01:03.940 --> 01:06.420
in fact, the last two
parties, we had 500 adults.

01:06.420 --> 01:11.725
At the last party, 200 of
them were men, and 300 of them

01:11.725 --> 01:12.225
were women.

01:15.070 --> 01:21.860
And in total, they ate
1,200 bags of potato chips.

01:21.860 --> 01:23.810
And you say, what about
the party before that?

01:23.810 --> 01:26.140
He says, that one, we had a
bigger skew towards women.

01:26.140 --> 01:31.190
We only had 100 men,
and we have 400 women.

01:33.700 --> 01:35.870
And that time, we
actually had fewer bags

01:35.870 --> 01:42.130
consumed-- 1,100
bags of potato chips.

01:42.130 --> 01:44.830
So you say, OK, king
and Arbegla, this

01:44.830 --> 01:47.020
seems like a fairly
straightforward thing.

01:47.020 --> 01:50.300
Let me define some variables
to represent our unknowns.

01:50.300 --> 01:51.830
So you go ahead
and you say, well,

01:51.830 --> 02:06.559
let's let m equal the number
of bags eaten by each man.

02:06.559 --> 02:08.100
And you could think
of it on average,

02:08.100 --> 02:09.878
or maybe all the
men in that kingdom

02:09.878 --> 02:10.919
are completely identical.

02:10.919 --> 02:14.410
Or maybe it's the average number
of bags eaten by each man.

02:14.410 --> 02:25.620
And let's let w equal the number
of bags eaten by each woman.

02:25.620 --> 02:28.960
And so with these
definitions of our variables,

02:28.960 --> 02:31.720
let's think about
how we can represent

02:31.720 --> 02:34.810
this first piece of information,
this piece of information

02:34.810 --> 02:36.940
in green.

02:36.940 --> 02:39.210
Well, let's think about
the total number of bags

02:39.210 --> 02:41.600
that the men ate.

02:41.600 --> 02:44.020
You had 200 men.

02:44.020 --> 02:45.390
Let me scroll over a little bit.

02:45.390 --> 02:50.750
You had 200 men, and they each
ate m bags, m bags per man.

02:50.750 --> 02:52.715
So the men at this
first party collectively

02:52.715 --> 02:55.150
ate 200 times m bags.

02:55.150 --> 02:58.640
If m is 10 bags per man,
then this would be 2,000.

02:58.640 --> 03:02.110
If m was 5 bags per man,
then this would be 5,000.

03:02.110 --> 03:04.610
We don't know what m
is, but 200 times m

03:04.610 --> 03:06.500
is the total eaten by the men.

03:06.500 --> 03:08.560
Same logic-- total
eaten by the women

03:08.560 --> 03:14.570
is 300 women times the number
of bags eaten by each woman.

03:14.570 --> 03:17.160
And so if you add the total to
eaten by the men and the women,

03:17.160 --> 03:22.200
you get the 1,200 bags.

03:22.200 --> 03:25.440
So this is information,
written algebraically,

03:25.440 --> 03:28.150
given these variable
definitions.

03:28.150 --> 03:30.812
Now, let's do the same
thing with the second part

03:30.812 --> 03:33.020
of the information that they
gave us right over here.

03:33.020 --> 03:35.436
Let's think about how we can
represent this algebraically.

03:37.850 --> 03:40.160
Well, similar logic--
what was a total

03:40.160 --> 03:42.070
that the men ate at that party?

03:42.070 --> 03:45.850
It was 100 men times
m bags per man.

03:45.850 --> 03:48.710
And we're assuming that m
is the same across parties,

03:48.710 --> 03:52.330
that men, on average, always
eat the same number of bags.

03:52.330 --> 03:54.820
And how many did the women
eat at that second party?

03:54.820 --> 03:56.460
Well, you had 400 women.

03:56.460 --> 04:00.140
And on average, they
ate w bags per woman.

04:00.140 --> 04:02.550
So this is 400 times
w is the total number

04:02.550 --> 04:03.620
that the women ate.

04:03.620 --> 04:05.850
You add those two together,
you get the total number

04:05.850 --> 04:07.150
that all the adults ate.

04:07.150 --> 04:11.680
So this is going
to be 1,100 bags.

04:11.680 --> 04:13.530
So it looks pretty similar now.

04:13.530 --> 04:17.190
You have a system of two
equations with two unknowns.

04:17.190 --> 04:21.430
And so you try your
best to solve it.

04:21.430 --> 04:23.680
But when you solve it, you
see something interesting.

04:23.680 --> 04:25.100
Last time, it was
very convenient.

04:25.100 --> 04:28.950
You had a, I think it was
a 500 here, for 500 adults,

04:28.950 --> 04:30.170
and you had another 500.

04:30.170 --> 04:31.650
And so it seemed
like it was pretty

04:31.650 --> 04:33.750
easy to cancel out
one of the variables.

04:33.750 --> 04:36.070
Here it seems a little
bit more difficult.

04:36.070 --> 04:38.660
What's multiplying by the
m's, it's different here.

04:38.660 --> 04:41.290
The coefficient on the w
is different over here.

04:41.290 --> 04:44.210
You say, well, maybe I can
change one of these equations

04:44.210 --> 04:46.670
so it makes it a little
bit easier to cancel out

04:46.670 --> 04:48.470
with the other equation.

04:48.470 --> 04:55.050
So what if, for example, I
were to take this blue equation

04:55.050 --> 04:58.760
right over here and
multiply it by negative 2?

04:58.760 --> 05:00.620
And you might say,
well, Sal, why are we

05:00.620 --> 05:01.870
multiplying it by negative 2?

05:01.870 --> 05:03.960
Well, if were to multiply
it by negative 2,

05:03.960 --> 05:07.790
this 100m would become
a negative 200m.

05:07.790 --> 05:10.190
And if it was a
negative 200m, then

05:10.190 --> 05:12.710
that would cancel out
with a positive 200m

05:12.710 --> 05:14.010
when we add the two.

05:14.010 --> 05:15.180
So let's see what happens.

05:15.180 --> 05:19.920
So let's multiply this blue
equation by negative 2.

05:19.920 --> 05:22.000
We're going to
multiply by negative 2.

05:22.000 --> 05:23.870
Let me scroll over to
the left a little bit.

05:23.870 --> 05:24.536
So what happens?

05:24.536 --> 05:27.630
Remember, when we
multiply an equation,

05:27.630 --> 05:29.380
we can't just do one
side of the equation.

05:29.380 --> 05:31.129
We have to do the
entire equation in order

05:31.129 --> 05:33.060
for the equality to hold true.

05:33.060 --> 05:38.060
So negative 2 times
100m is negative 200m.

05:38.060 --> 05:41.660
Negative 2 times 400w-- there's
a positive right over there.

05:41.660 --> 05:44.810
So it becomes negative 800w.

05:44.810 --> 05:47.370
And then negative 2-- now,
we did the left hand side,

05:47.370 --> 05:49.360
but we also have to do
the right hand side.

05:49.360 --> 05:55.120
Negative 2 times 1,100
is negative 2,200.

05:55.120 --> 05:56.895
So just to be
clear, this equation

05:56.895 --> 05:58.470
that I just wrote
here essentially

05:58.470 --> 06:00.680
has the same information
we just manipulated.

06:00.680 --> 06:03.400
We just changed this equation,
multiplied both sides

06:03.400 --> 06:04.410
by negative 2.

06:04.410 --> 06:06.672
But it's kind of
the same constraint.

06:06.672 --> 06:08.130
But what makes this
interesting is,

06:08.130 --> 06:10.690
now, we can rewrite
this green equation.

06:10.690 --> 06:13.200
Let me do it over
here, this first one.

06:13.200 --> 06:20.835
200m plus 300w is
equal to 1,200.

06:20.835 --> 06:22.960
And the whole reason why
I multiplied by negative 2

06:22.960 --> 06:25.090
is, so that if I were
to add these two things,

06:25.090 --> 06:27.810
I might be able to get rid
of that variable over there.

06:27.810 --> 06:28.862
And so let's do that.

06:28.862 --> 06:31.320
Let's add the left hand sides,
and let's add the right hand

06:31.320 --> 06:31.880
sides.

06:31.880 --> 06:33.588
And you could literally
view it as, we're

06:33.588 --> 06:35.360
starting with this
blue equation.

06:35.360 --> 06:37.970
We're adding this
quantity, the left hand

06:37.970 --> 06:40.770
side of the yellow equation to
the left hand side of the blue.

06:40.770 --> 06:42.632
And then 1,200 is
the exact same thing

06:42.632 --> 06:44.340
that we're adding to
the right hand side.

06:44.340 --> 06:46.270
We know that this
is equal to this.

06:46.270 --> 06:48.740
So we can add this to the
left hand side and this

06:48.740 --> 06:50.170
to the right hand side.

06:50.170 --> 06:51.592
So let's see what happens.

06:51.592 --> 06:53.300
So the good thing is,
the whole reason we

06:53.300 --> 06:55.300
multiplied it by negative
2, so that these two

06:55.300 --> 06:56.336
characters cancel out.

06:56.336 --> 06:57.460
You add those two together.

06:57.460 --> 06:59.870
You just get 0m or just 0.

06:59.870 --> 07:03.990
You have negative
800w plus 300w.

07:03.990 --> 07:06.881
Well, that's negative 500w.

07:06.881 --> 07:08.380
And then on the
right hand side, you

07:08.380 --> 07:11.140
have negative 2,200 plus 1,200.

07:11.140 --> 07:14.544
So that's negative 1,000.

07:14.544 --> 07:16.210
And now this is pretty
straightforward--

07:16.210 --> 07:18.460
one equation, one unknown,
a fairly straightforward

07:18.460 --> 07:19.230
equation.

07:19.230 --> 07:22.920
We divide both sides by
the coefficient of w,

07:22.920 --> 07:23.930
multiplying w.

07:23.930 --> 07:28.570
So divide by negative 500 on
the left, divide by negative 500

07:28.570 --> 07:29.500
on the right.

07:29.500 --> 07:34.750
And we are left with
w is equal to 2.

07:34.750 --> 07:38.440
On average, women ate
two bags of potato chips

07:38.440 --> 07:39.270
at these parties.

07:39.270 --> 07:42.080
We're assuming that's
constant across the parties.

07:42.080 --> 07:44.280
So let's think about how
you would then figure out

07:44.280 --> 07:48.810
how many bags, on
average, each man ate.

07:48.810 --> 07:51.026
Well, to do that,
we just go back

07:51.026 --> 07:52.400
to either one of
these equations.

07:52.400 --> 07:55.850
In the last set of videos, I
went to the first equation.

07:55.850 --> 07:58.200
I'll show that the second
equation should also work.

07:58.200 --> 07:59.660
Either one should work.

07:59.660 --> 08:01.765
So let's substitute back
into the second equation.

08:01.765 --> 08:04.140
And you could either pick this
version of it or this one.

08:04.140 --> 08:05.850
But I'll pick the original one.

08:05.850 --> 08:09.190
So you have 100
times m, which we're

08:09.190 --> 08:12.400
trying to figure out,
plus 400 times-- well,

08:12.400 --> 08:16.010
we now know that w is
equal to 2-- 400 times

08:16.010 --> 08:21.610
2 is equal to 1,100.

08:21.610 --> 08:28.950
So you have 100m plus
800 is equal to 1,100.

08:28.950 --> 08:32.000
And now, to solve for
m, we could subtract 800

08:32.000 --> 08:32.685
from both sides.

08:36.650 --> 08:43.890
And we are left with
100m is equal to 300.

08:43.890 --> 08:49.690
And now, divide
both sides by 100.

08:49.690 --> 08:53.490
And we are left with m, which
is, on average, the number

08:53.490 --> 08:57.940
of bags of chips each
man eats is equal to 3.

08:57.940 --> 09:00.490
So you have solved
Arbegla's problem,

09:00.490 --> 09:03.220
what he thought was a
difficult problem, using

09:03.220 --> 09:06.000
the magical, mystical
powers of algebra.

09:06.000 --> 09:09.780
You were able to tell the king
in his party planning process

09:09.780 --> 09:12.080
that, on average,
the men will eat

09:12.080 --> 09:14.860
three bags of potato chips each.

09:14.860 --> 09:16.930
And on average,
the women will eat

09:16.930 --> 09:20.510
two bags of potato chips each.
